OL,3,GNEWSAStunning partial eclipse
OL,4,Aphotographs from Sussex
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe August full moon, also known as the
OL,7,FSturgeon Moon, lit up the sky on
OL,8,FThursday night and was photographed by
OL,9,FSussex Weather Watchers.
OL,11,FThe Sun, Earth and Moon also lined up
OL,12,Fin the night sky to create a lunar
OL,13,Feclipse in parts of the world.
OL,15,FThe partial eclipse was visible across
OL,16,Fthe South East from 02:23 BST until
OL,17,F06:51. And in many areas, the Moon took
OL,18,Fon a reddish appearance.
OL,20,FThe next lunar eclipse visible in the
OL,21,FUK will be in February 2027.
OL,23,APub: 28-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
